; 42-sym.kurt

; `sym OP` declares an infix operator symmetric: its arguments may be swapped
; without changing the formula, as far as Kurt's matching is concerned.  This
; matters when Kurt searches the theory for something to match against --
; without it, `b + a` and `a + b` would be treated as unrelated formulas.

infix "+" 20 20
sym "+"

var a, b
use a + b
b + a                 ; matches the axiom above even though the order differs

; `=` (11-def.kurt, `equality.kurt`) and `and`/`or` (`prop.kurt`) are all
; declared `sym` for exactly this reason.
